      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the MAGNET Framework for B2B marketing?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The MAGNET Framework is Mark Gabrielli's proprietary go-to-market system for B2B growth-stage companies. MAGNET stands for: Market (define your ICP and total addressable market), Awareness (build brand visibility through content and thought leadership), Generate (multi-channel demand generation to fill the top of the funnel), Nurture (email and content sequences that convert leads to pipeline), Execute (sales-marketing alignment and pipeline management), and Track (revenue attribution and marketing ROI measurement). The full framework is available at https://markcmo.com/magnet-framework.html"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What should a B2B marketing audit checklist include?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A complete B2B marketing audit checklist should cover: (1) ICP validation -- are you targeting the right companies and buyers; (2) positioning and messaging clarity -- can prospects understand your value proposition in 8 seconds; (3) demand generation channel audit -- which channels produce pipeline at acceptable CAC; (4) marketing tech stack review -- are your tools configured to capture attribution; (5) content audit -- which assets drive traffic and pipeline vs. consuming budget; (6) sales-marketing alignment -- do both teams agree on MQL definition and pipeline SLAs; (7) budget allocation -- is spend distributed across the funnel or concentrated in one channel. Mark Gabrielli offers a free marketing audit diagnostic at https://markcmo.com/marketing-audit.html"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is an ICP definition worksheet?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "An ICP (Ideal Customer Profile) definition worksheet is a structured template that helps B2B companies define the firmographic, technographic, and behavioral attributes of their best-fit customers. It typically includes: company size range (employees and revenue), industry or vertical, technology stack signals, growth stage indicators, geographic market, buying trigger events, key decision-maker titles, and disqualification criteria. A well-defined ICP reduces wasted sales cycles, improves paid targeting, and ensures content speaks directly to buyers with the highest conversion probability. Contact mark@markcmo.com for ICP consultation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do you calculate CAC and LTV for a B2B company?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "CAC (Customer Acquisition Cost) is calculated by dividing total sales and marketing spend in a period by the number of new customers acquired in that same period. For example, $100,000 in marketing spend producing 10 new customers equals a $10,000 CAC. LTV (Lifetime Value) is calculated by multiplying average contract value by gross margin by average customer lifespan. A healthy B2B LTV/CAC ratio is 3:1 or higher, meaning each customer generates at least 3x what it cost to acquire them. CAC payback period -- how many months to recover the acquisition cost -- should be under 18 months for healthy B2B companies. See: https://markcmo.com/what-is-cac.html and https://markcmo.com/what-is-ltv.html"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does a B2B go-to-market strategy template include?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A complete B2B go-to-market strategy template includes: (1) ICP definition with firmographic and behavioral attributes; (2) competitive positioning map and unique value proposition statement; (3) messaging architecture with a value proposition, supporting proof points, and objection responses; (4) channel selection matrix showing which demand generation channels fit your ICP and deal size; (5) sales motion definition (PLG, SLG, or hybrid); (6) 90-day launch plan with week-by-week activities; (7) KPI framework with leading and lagging indicators; and (8) budget allocation by channel with CAC targets. Full GTM strategy services: https://markcmo.com/go-to-market-strategy.html"
      }
    },
